# flow-offload/firewall.snippet
#
# Drop-in UCI addition for /etc/config/firewall on the R8000 (bcm53xx).
# Apply by appending to the existing `config defaults` section, or by
# `uci import` / `uci batch` (see NOTES.md for exact install steps).
#
# WHY software (not hardware) offload:
# bcm53xx (BCM4709 / Northstar, R8000's SoC) has no upstream hardware NAT
# acceleration path. Stock Netgear firmware uses Broadcom's proprietary CTF /
# "NATP accelerator" to hit line-rate; that block is not driven by the
# mainline b53/bgmac drivers OpenWrt uses. Confirmed by a bcm53xx maintainer
# on a sibling Northstar board (Linksys EA9500, same switch family as R8000's
# BCM53012 SRAB switch):
#   "the stock firmware makes use of the NATP accelerator, whereas the
#    upstream kernel or OpenWrt does not have that capability"
#   -- https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/7023#issuecomment-1040297058
# The same thread's resolution for reaching line-rate on this exact switch
# family is CPU-based "software flow-offloading" in firewall settings:
#   https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/7023#issuecomment-1040297068
#
# flow_offloading_hw is left OFF on purpose -- there is no hw offload path on
# this target and forcing it on is a silent no-op at best.

config defaults
	option syn_flood		'1'
	option input			'REJECT'
	option output			'ACCEPT'
	option forward			'REJECT'
	option flow_offloading		'1'
	option flow_offloading_hw	'0'
